tuntap_bb: make BB_SOCK_FLAG_DATAGRAM a runtime choice, default on

bb_socket_open()'s DATAGRAM bit used to always reach this host's own
chip masked away (see 0008-session_socket-preserve-datagram-flag-on-open.patch
for why that mattered: it left this end's chip always non-datagram
while the camera's netif, on the OpenIPC/builder air side, was always
datagram -- a per-chip mode mismatch that broke the RF link's netif
bridging outright). With that fixed, both ends can actually agree on
DATAGRAM, which is what this tool already hardcoded upstream -- so
default it back on, but keep it a runtime flag (-g/--no-datagram to
turn it off) instead of hardcoding one assumption, since testing
non-datagram (its own tradeoff: no length-prefix framing, and a hard
~718-byte per-write ceiling confirmed live via `ping -s`) shouldn't
need a patch+rebuild cycle each time.

diff --git a/dev_helper/tuntap_bb/test_bb_tun.h b/dev_helper/tuntap_bb/test_bb_tun.h
